{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:20710-1","published":"2026-03-09T10:51:06Z","modified":"2026-03-23T04:53:09.262343Z","related":["CVE-2025-11468","CVE-2025-12781","CVE-2025-15282","CVE-2025-15366","CVE-2025-15367","CVE-2026-0672","CVE-2026-0865"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-11468","CVE-2025-12781","CVE-2025-15282","CVE-2025-15366","CVE-2025-15367","CVE-2026-0672","CVE-2026-0865"],"summary":"Security update for python311","details":"This update for python311 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2025-11468: preserving parens when folding comments in email headers. (bsc#1257029)\n- CVE-2026-0672: rejects control characters in http cookies. (bsc#1257031)\n- CVE-2026-0865: rejecting control characters in wsgiref.headers.Headers, which could be abused for injecting false HTTP headers. (bsc#1257042)\n- CVE-2025-15366: basically the same as the previous patch for IMAP protocol. (bsc#1257044)\n- CVE-2025-15282: basically the same as the previous patch for urllib library. (bsc#1257046)\n- CVE-2025-15367: basically the same as the previous patch for poplib library. (bsc#1257041)\n- CVE-2025-12781: fix decoding with non-standard Base64 alphabet (bsc#1257108)\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python311","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Micro 6.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python311&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Micro%206.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.11.14-3.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libpython3_11-1_0":"3.11.14-3.1","python311":"3.11.14-3.1","python311-base":"3.11.14-3.1","python311-curses":"3.11.14-3.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:20710-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"python311-core","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Micro 6.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python311-core&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Micro%206.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.11.14-3.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libpython3_11-1_0":"3.11.14-3.1","python311":"3.11.14-3.1","p